    "result": "I implemented `search_products` in `solution.py` and wrote a 31-case pytest suite in `tests/test_solution.py`; `python -m pytest -q tests` passes. The function validates `order_by`, `limit` and `offset` before querying, then runs one parameterised SELECT. Stock filtering, the optional price cap, and ordering with `id` ascending as the tie-breaker are all in that query. Substring matching uses `instr(lower(name), lower(?))`, which is literal, so `%` and `_` are ordinary characters, and case folding is ASCII-only as the spec says. Results are built as `{id, name, price}` dicts, and the function only ever runs SELECTs, so the database is never modified. Two of my first test expectations were wrong (the binary-order first name and the descending price order), and I corrected them against the spec rather than changing the implementation.",
